+/* One smoothed DM-RS pilot: raised-cosine FIR over the neighbouring pilots of
+ * the same CDM group, with the per-pilot phase step removed first.
+ *
+ * A timing offset rotates the channel linearly across frequency. Averaging
+ * rotated taps shrinks the estimate and the residual is then counted as noise
+ * (SINR -2.5 dB at 1 PRB, -0.6 dB at 6 PRB with 1 us, D8). The step is
+ * estimated inside the filter window, the taps are de-rotated about the output
+ * pilot and filtered, so the output keeps its own phase -- the CPU estimator
+ * reaches the same end with unwrapped-phase virtual pilots. Out-of-range taps
+ * are skipped and the filter renormalised, which also makes one PRB safe.
+ *
+ * Tap t of pilot q lives at sym_base + (q / nof_pilots) * prb_stride + inner +
+ * pusch_dmrs_sc_offset(dmrs_type, cdm, q % nof_pilots). */
